{"name":"Ballroom Slippers","hex":"#85928e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ballroom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large room used for dancing and banquets.","A type of elegant dance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take part in ballroom dancing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ballroom"},{"term":"slippers","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of slipper"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of slipper"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slippers"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ballroom","blocks":[{"text":"A ballroom or ballhall is a large room for holding large formal parties called balls. Traditionally, most balls were held in private residences; many mansions and palaces, especially historic mansions and palaces, contain one or more ballrooms. In other large houses, a large room such as the main drawing room, long gallery, or hall may double as a ballroom, but a good ballroom should have the right type of flooring, such as hardwood flooring or stone flooring .. For most styles of modern dance, a wooden sprung floor offers the best surface."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Catherine_Palace_ballroom.jpg/330px-Catherine_Palace_ballroom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballroom","wikidata":"Q805353"},{"title":"Slipper","blocks":[{"text":"Slippers are a type of shoes falling under the broader category of light footwear, that are easy to put on and off and are intended to be worn indoors, particularly at home. They provide comfort and protection for the feet when walking indoors."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Slippers.jpg/330px-Slippers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slipper","wikidata":"Q876824"}],"images":[{